    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n45347" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">εὔτροπος</span></b> , <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ον</span>,
			(<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τρέπω</span>) <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>versatile</i>, etym. of <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">εὐτράπελος</span>, <i><span class="en">
				Arist.
				<u>EN</u>
				1128a10
			</span></i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>II.</b> (<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τρόπος</span>) <i>morally good</i>, Sch.<i><span class="en">
				Od.
				1.1
			</span></i>; of diseases, <i>mild</i>, 
			<i><span class="en">
				Hp.
				<u>Hum.</u>
				13
			</span></i>; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">εὔτροπος ἀνθρώποισι
			δαίμων</span> dub. sens. in <i><span class="en">
				<u>PHib.</u>
				1.2.6
			</span></i> (cf. <i><span class="en">
				Epich.
				258
			</span></i>). Adv. -<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">πως</span>, 
				gloss on 
				<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">εὐοργήτως</span>
			, Sch.<i><span class="en">
				Th.
				1.122
			</span></i>.</div>
